-A method encoding spatial coherence into a pyramid of binary volumes. It solves the problem of inefficiently traversing large voxel datasets by allowing rays to skip large empty regions in logarithmic time relative to ray length. Unlike geometric ray tracing which uses bounding volumes or condensed octree representations, this method uses a complete octree structure (pyramid of binary volumes) specifically optimized for the spatially ordered, single-sample nature of volume data.
