 ### [Flex-block tree](9716-flex-block-tree.md)
-A hierarchical data structure derived from a kd-tree, designed to distribute massive volume data across distributed rendering nodes while ensuring load balancing and deterministic view-dependent ordering. It solves the problem of efficient data distribution and ray-task scheduling in distributed ray casting and ray tracing by partitioning space into "flex-blocks" that tightly crop empty space. Unlike traditional space subdivision methods that alternate axis cuts, the flex-block partition allows flexible cut orientations to accommodate scenes with disproportionate dimensions, and it provides a dependency graph for image composition in ray casting and traversal acceleration in ray tracing.
