 ### [Spatial Hierarchies](13154-spatial-hierarchies.md)
-Accelerate volume rendering by performing point location through recursive search through the tree structure. They organize spatial data into a hierarchy of bounding volumes, allowing the renderer to quickly cull empty or irrelevant regions. What sets them apart from sibling methods like Hierarchical Spatial Enumeration Optimization is their explicit geometric subdivision of space rather than linear enumeration or silhouette-based approximations.
