 ### [Brick-of-Bricks Decomposition](13647-brick-of-bricks-decomposition.md)
-A storage format for volume data where the volume is stored as a flat hierarchy of bricks of size $n^3$ to improve cache-coherence in volume traversal. It arises from not fully expanding an octree into single-voxel leaf nodes. It sets itself apart from fully expanded octrees by maintaining a hierarchical structure of larger blocks rather than individual voxels, and from flat grids by providing spatial locality through block-based indexing.
